  "_comment": "Sprite sources -> Build tiles. Run: python tools/mksprite.py [name]. Each group fills a tile range from the one source image: height = tile height in pixels (Duke's own sizes keep the in-game scale), squash = scale height only (crouch/dive), rotate = degrees clockwise (falling over / lying dead), flip = mirror top to bottom, view = which view of a sheet (default 0, front), per_view = the range is Duke's frame*5+view layout (each tile takes view (tile - first) % 5). A source can be a turnaround sheet: views = how many figures side by side (front, 3/4 front, side, 3/4 back, back), mirror = views drawn facing right (Duke's turned views face left). Optional per entry: bg_tol (how far from the background colour still counts as background, default 40), shadow_depth (how much darker than the background a grey shadow can be, default 60), max_lum (drop pale greyish pixels brighter than this: glow/haze around a dark figure).",
